Absolutely. The key is to **stop treating this as “convert Foundationary”** and instead treat it as a **full frontend rebuild of PlanningIndex, using Foundationary only as the technical starting point**.

The transformation should happen in **strict phases**. Bolt should never be asked to build the whole thing at once.

# PlanningIndex — Complete Frontend Rebuild Plan

## 0. The fundamental rule

The new project is:

> **PlanningIndex rebuilt from the ground up, using the existing Foundationary codebase as the frontend foundation.**

Foundationary is **not** being redesigned.

It is being **removed conceptually and visually**.

The existing Foundationary project gives us useful infrastructure such as:

* Next.js/React structure
* Tailwind/design system
* routing
* authentication foundations
* Stripe foundations
* client-side application structure
* admin/client concepts
* reusable UI components
* Vercel deployment
* GitHub workflow

But the finished product must contain **zero Foundationary identity**.

No:

* Foundationary terminology
* Foundationary documents
* Foundationary questionnaire
* Foundationary business logic
* Foundationary branding
* Foundationary marketing
* Foundationary database
* Foundationary-specific workflows

The final product should feel as though **PlanningIndex was always built in this application**.

---

# 1. The architecture we are building

The frontend should ultimately look conceptually like this:

```text
                    PLANNINGINDEX.CO.UK
                            │
             ┌──────────────┴──────────────┐
             │                             │
             ▼                             ▼
       PUBLIC WEBSITE                  APPLICATION
             │                             │
      ┌──────┼───────┐             ┌───────┼────────┐
      │      │       │             │       │        │
     Home  Features  Pricing      Search    CRM    Proposals
      │      │       │             │       │        │
    About  Contact  Blog          Maps    Leads   Mail
    Help                         Filters  Notes   Tracking
```

The frontend lives on Vercel.

The existing backend remains elsewhere.

```text
                    NEXT.JS
                       │
                       │ HTTPS
                       ▼
              EXISTING BACKEND/API
                       │
          ┌────────────┼─────────────┐
          ▼            ▼             ▼
       Planning      Users         PMPro
        Data                       Stripe
          │
       Scraper
```

**The frontend does not own the planning database.**

The frontend does not become responsible for scraping.

The frontend does not create a second planning database.

The frontend simply becomes a vastly better interface to the existing PlanningIndex infrastructure.

